    schema:description "Your role FRASER is an independent creative agency with teams across Berlin, Zurich, Cape Town and Dubai. We develop integrated campaigns, content and digital experiences for ambitious international brands, combining strategic thinking, creativity and technology. As our Accountant, you will play a key role in keeping FRASER's day-to-day finance operations running smoothly. You will work closely with our Finance Manager and external accounting and tax partners across our international locations. Your responsibilities will include: Manage day-to-day accounting and financial administration Process, verify and organise incoming and outgoing invoices, including accurate allocation to projects and entities Maintain accurate financial records across our accounting and ERP systems Prepare bookkeeping documentation and support monthly closing and reconciliation processes Coordinate payment runs, recurring expenses and subscriptions Work closely with external accountants and tax advisors across our international entities Identify discrepancies and support the Finance Manager with day-to-day finance tasks and reporting Your profile 4+ years of experience in accounting, bookkeeping or a similar finance role Solid experience working with German accounting and financial processes Hands-on experience with DATEV and ERP/accounting systems Good understanding of German bookkeeping principles Experience with invoice processing, reconciliations, accounts payable and general accounting Strong attention to detail and a structured, organised way of working Comfortable working independently and taking ownership of recurring financial processes Experience working with multiple entities or international businesses is a plus Professional working proficiency in German (B2 or above) Excellent English, both written and spoken A pragmatic, hands-on approach and the ability to work effectively in a fast-paced, entrepreneurial environment What we offer The opportunity to shape a globally relevant social media arm of a growing agency with relevant big clients and substantial business A senior leadership team that is close and passionately ambitious Fantastic colleagues and a collaborative environment Competitive salary Employee benefits program Chance to help shape the agency and influence its growth Flat hierarchy fostering a transparent and collaborative work culture International environment with diverse employees, clients, and locations Experienced team: work alongside seasoned professionals 30 days of vacation per year (based on a 5-day workweek) Opportunity for workation from European countries or South Africa Flexible working hours and locations, including 3 days on site in our great office and 2 home office A great roof terrace in the heart of Kreuzberg and always a fridge full of cool drinks Find more English Speaking Jobs in Germany on Arbeitnow" ;
